{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKviQ6WMNwDDBXtwmyz6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the plan to `.ard/138/plan.md` and the role file to `.ard/138/triage-engineer.md`, with status done. I have not built or tested anything, because this was planning only.\n\nThe plan takes the issue's preferred route: at commit time, replace only the job's own `plan.md` section in the current `main` copy. If that copy can't be merged safely, the job fails closed to `needs-human`.\n\nThe committer currently writes the job's whole file onto the latest `main`, and nothing guards that for these commits. So the merge has to run inside the committer's attempt step, where each push retry re-fetches `main`. A merge done earlier in close-out could go stale on a retry.\n\nThe plan has six steps:\n- an optional merge hook on the committer's file type\n- a new `ErrMerge` error\n- a new `mergeOwnSection` in `internal/closeout`\n- wiring it into `Closer.commit`\n- mapping merge failure to `needs-human`\n- a \"Who may write what\" paragraph in `docs/proposal.md`\n\nThe test plan includes the regression case the issue asks for, where another role's section changes on `main` between the job's base and its commit.\n\nSize M, risk medium. The risk comes from changing the shared committer file type and its retry loop, which other callers use. The hook is optional, so existing callers are unaffected, and no protected paths are touched.\n\nTwo open items are in the comment. The worker should check how the existing allowlist-denial path in `prepare.go` keeps only the log and role file, and reuse it for the merge-failure case. A maintainer may also want to confirm the rebase-over-fail approach.\n\nAn earlier command of mine created an empty `.ard/138/plan.md` before I wrote the real plan into it. The file now holds the full plan."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"in